WEBVTT

00:01.610 --> 00:10.400
Continuing their journey towards the Eisetsu Gym in order to get the eighth badge, Satoshi and his friends have stopped by a Pokémon Center in a forest.

00:02.980 --> 00:12.830
While watching anime, make sure not to sit too close to the screen and that the room is well lit.

00:26.260 --> 00:27.540
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:28.700 --> 00:30.340
Everyone has recovered.

00:32.760 --> 00:33.790
Welcome back, Pikachu.

00:38.050 --> 00:39.250
What do you wanna do now, Citron?

00:39.540 --> 00:40.620
Let me think...

00:40.980 --> 00:43.010
Shall we rest for a while longer before we go?

00:43.320 --> 00:43.700
Good idea.

00:45.300 --> 00:46.900
Eievui, what do you think? Does it feel nice?

00:58.720 --> 01:00.120
Wait for your turn!

01:00.760 --> 01:02.280
If you don't behave, I won't groom you!

01:08.680 --> 01:10.340
All right, you're next, Tairenar.

01:14.660 --> 01:15.800
All right, done!

01:16.320 --> 01:17.880
You all look neat now.

01:19.850 --> 01:22.680
Oh, right. Let's check for new PokéVisions.

01:26.540 --> 01:28.400
Hm? What could this be?

01:32.140 --> 01:34.240
Bonjour to all Performers.

01:34.840 --> 01:38.860
Mesdemoiselles who're doing their best with their performances by utilizing cute elegance,

01:39.580 --> 01:44.580
today I invite you to a dance party hosted by me, Pierre!

01:45.240 --> 01:45.790
What?

01:49.470 --> 01:55.170
Satoshi and Serena!
Getting One at a Dance Party!!

01:55.520 --> 01:58.320
...a dance party hosted by me, Pierre!

01:58.870 --> 01:59.930
A dance party?

02:00.560 --> 02:04.890
This will provide a tiny little break for you Performers who always compete on stage.

02:05.250 --> 02:07.270
Please look forward to it.

02:08.030 --> 02:09.070
Wow.

02:09.070 --> 02:10.390
That sounds fun!

02:10.710 --> 02:14.510
However, this party has one condition.

02:11.100 --> 02:21.000
Play a board game via the Pocket Monsters XY& data broadcast!
Press the d-button on your remote and try reaching the battles and the presents!!

02:11.100 --> 02:21.000
Z

02:18.210 --> 02:23.730
All attendees, Performers and Pokémon alike, will register in pairs of one male and one female.

02:26.270 --> 02:28.470
Wow, pairs of one male and one female, huh?

02:30.690 --> 02:34.590
I'm sure it's going to be an elegant and très bien party.

02:34.590 --> 02:35.760
Also,

02:35.760 --> 02:38.710
Kalos Queen Elle will also be attending as a guest.

02:39.440 --> 02:40.220
Elle-san too?

02:40.670 --> 02:43.090
Now then, let's meet at the venue.

02:45.860 --> 02:47.810
Serena, let's go, let's go!

02:48.230 --> 02:49.270
Of course you're going! Aren't you?

02:51.110 --> 02:51.570
Yeah.

02:54.110 --> 02:55.360
Eievui, do you want to give it a try?

02:56.290 --> 02:57.950
I think there will be a lot of people there, but...

02:58.470 --> 02:59.650
...I'm sure it'll be a great experience for you.

03:01.860 --> 03:03.750
They said pairs of one male and one female...

03:04.110 --> 03:05.920
Pokémon have to come in pairs too, right?

03:05.920 --> 03:07.090
How about Horubee, then?

03:08.310 --> 03:09.120
I see.

03:09.890 --> 03:10.520
Please come out.

03:13.070 --> 03:16.720
Horubee, will you go to the dance party together with Eievui?

03:18.340 --> 03:20.350
Can I ask you to be Eievui's partner?

03:23.140 --> 03:25.050
Does that mean you and my brother will go as a pair?

03:25.990 --> 03:27.030
Uh...

03:28.420 --> 03:29.930
Citron, can you...?

03:30.370 --> 03:32.100
M-Me?!

03:33.120 --> 03:34.390
Do your best, Citron!

03:35.780 --> 03:36.940
I will try...

03:37.350 --> 03:40.210
But will it be all right with me involved...?

03:40.210 --> 03:41.230
It'll be fine, I'm sure of it!

03:43.330 --> 03:47.280
Eievui, let's show everyone your lovely dance.

03:52.550 --> 03:54.430
It seems to be around here...

04:03.110 --> 04:06.160
Oh, it sure is lively!

04:07.630 --> 04:09.570
You're right, there are lots of people!

04:10.070 --> 04:11.550
Bro, will you be all right?

04:11.930 --> 04:12.930
Will I?

04:13.170 --> 04:14.690
I feel very uneasy.

04:15.350 --> 04:16.630
Please bear with me, Citron.

04:17.010 --> 04:20.210
Oh... So your partner <i>isn't</i> Satoshi, Serena?

04:22.310 --> 04:23.490
Millefeui!

04:23.490 --> 04:24.420
It's been a while.

04:26.470 --> 04:27.790
It really has.

04:29.750 --> 04:31.450
I didn't know you and your friends were here too, Serena.

04:31.860 --> 04:35.390
You came just at the right time. I was getting worried because I couldn't find a partner.

04:36.160 --> 04:39.620
If you're free, Satoshi, can't you become my partner?

04:39.620 --> 04:39.960
What?!

04:40.560 --> 04:41.890
If it's fine with you, then sure.

04:42.190 --> 04:43.170
What?!

04:43.620 --> 04:45.270
Thank you, Satoshi!

04:49.150 --> 04:50.740
You've got an Eievui, right?

04:52.550 --> 04:55.590
Yeah. You'll be surprised when you see this little one perform!

04:55.990 --> 04:57.310
It's a very good dancer, after all!

04:58.070 --> 05:00.160
I saw it in the Tripokalon the other day!

05:00.820 --> 05:01.990
It should become a good rival.

05:02.400 --> 05:05.380
But for today, let's enjoy the party!

05:18.370 --> 05:20.380
Geez, Millefeui...!

05:21.860 --> 05:23.120
Let's go too!

05:30.930 --> 05:33.940
I didn't think the brats would come as well...

05:33.940 --> 05:36.480
This is a good chance to go after Pikachu.

05:38.080 --> 05:43.740
The one most worthy to be the star of today's party is me, as I possess both attractiveness and grace.

05:44.270 --> 05:47.270
Huh? You don't wanna get Pikachu?

05:48.640 --> 05:51.070
Kojiro, escort me already.

05:51.070 --> 05:52.980
O-Oui, Mademoiselle.

05:57.520 --> 05:59.430
The pair of Millefeui-san and Satoshi-san...

05:59.860 --> 06:01.590
...and the pair of Serena-san and Citron-san...

06:01.870 --> 06:03.110
...have been registered.

06:03.520 --> 06:05.500
Also, please take these.

06:07.620 --> 06:08.590
What are these?

06:09.250 --> 06:11.490
You will need these cards during the party.

06:12.190 --> 06:15.470
You can rent costumes over there, so please help yourselves.

06:17.110 --> 06:18.590
Whoa!

06:25.890 --> 06:27.940
That's a lot of dresses!

06:28.340 --> 06:29.490
You are right.

06:33.920 --> 06:35.460
Oh, this one's lovely!

06:35.860 --> 06:37.510
Hm... This one and...

06:37.510 --> 06:37.970
...this one too!

06:39.120 --> 06:40.530
Oh, that one's nice too!

06:40.720 --> 06:41.840
You still wanna try on more?

06:51.410 --> 06:53.110
Serena, you look so cute!

06:53.110 --> 06:55.150
Eureka, yours looks perfect on you too!

06:56.100 --> 06:57.100
It's nice, isn't it?

07:02.790 --> 07:04.190
Oh, there she is!

07:05.380 --> 07:06.580
Sorry to keep you waiting!

07:08.590 --> 07:10.610
Hm... I've got to hand it to you; you've got taste.

07:11.270 --> 07:12.190
You too, Millefeui.

07:12.630 --> 07:14.610
Urgh, these clothes are really tight...

07:15.190 --> 07:17.120
We are not used to wearing this kind of thing, after all.

07:30.150 --> 07:31.050
It's Elle-san.

07:31.950 --> 07:34.190
Ladies and gentlemen!

07:34.190 --> 07:38.580
Thank you for coming to my dance party today.

07:40.000 --> 07:45.250
Let me introduce today's special guest, Kalos Queen Elle!

07:45.830 --> 07:47.190
Hello, everyone.

07:57.840 --> 07:59.350
Just watch me.

07:59.350 --> 08:02.390
I'll take away your title of Kalos Queen for sure.

08:25.140 --> 08:26.070
She's so lovely...

08:26.070 --> 08:26.910
She really is.

08:27.360 --> 08:29.560
That woman is our goal, right?

08:50.660 --> 08:53.910
Everyone, now begins the long-awaited free time.

08:54.210 --> 08:55.880
Please have a wonderful time.

08:56.580 --> 08:57.890
Come on, let's dance.

08:58.150 --> 08:58.670
Yeah!

08:59.780 --> 09:01.380
Citron, I'll count on you.

09:01.380 --> 09:01.890
O-Okay.

09:16.270 --> 09:16.790
One.

09:17.300 --> 09:17.630
Okay!

09:18.770 --> 09:19.380
Two.

09:19.670 --> 09:20.150
Okay!

09:21.140 --> 09:21.760
Three.

09:22.070 --> 09:22.360
Okay!

09:24.150 --> 09:25.630
Bro, do your best!

09:31.130 --> 09:31.730
Oops!

09:31.730 --> 09:33.440
Geez, are you all right?

09:35.780 --> 09:36.660
Sorry.

09:39.350 --> 09:40.720
Ow!

09:43.870 --> 09:44.710
I'm sorry.

09:45.070 --> 09:47.090
Satoshi, is it possible that you...?

09:51.920 --> 09:53.330
Eievui, what do you think?

09:55.030 --> 09:55.480
Thank goodness.

10:00.720 --> 10:03.890
Watch my magnificent dance.

10:05.570 --> 10:07.630
Un, deux! Un, deux! Un, deux, trois!

10:09.040 --> 10:09.830
Again!

10:10.370 --> 10:11.500
Un, deux! Un, deux!

10:14.470 --> 10:16.080
All these people here...

10:16.770 --> 10:18.310
...are aiming to become Kalos Queen.

10:19.350 --> 10:20.880
We have to do our best as well!

10:22.630 --> 10:25.030
Now then, everyone, please form a circle.

10:26.510 --> 10:29.990
We will now proceed with partner rotation dancing.

10:36.500 --> 10:37.910
Now then, let the music...

10:38.690 --> 10:39.490
...start!

10:47.310 --> 10:50.440
I wonder if Eievui will be all right with a partner that isn't Horubee.

10:57.230 --> 10:58.020
Thank goodness.

11:05.490 --> 11:06.640
You're struggling, huh?

11:06.880 --> 11:07.390
Elle-san!

11:08.270 --> 11:09.860
Relax, relax!

11:09.860 --> 11:10.350
Okay.

11:13.920 --> 11:16.000
Why do I have to do this...?

11:17.650 --> 11:20.270
Those were wonderful moves, Mademoiselle.

11:20.560 --> 11:21.650
Thank you very much.

11:51.750 --> 11:53.040
What?!

11:53.700 --> 11:55.010
Oh, it's over, huh?

11:55.540 --> 11:57.070
Serena, did you have fun?

11:57.070 --> 11:58.340
Y-Yeah...

11:58.880 --> 12:01.030
I guess I wanted to dance a little more.

12:01.590 --> 12:04.260
Now then, today's main event...

12:04.580 --> 12:06.430
...is a captivating tag battle.

12:06.990 --> 12:12.640
Pokémon battles don't occur in Tripokalons, so this is a special surprise!

12:13.550 --> 12:15.990
The participants of the battle will be determined via lottery.

12:16.370 --> 12:21.270
Please hold up the cards you received at the registration towards the chandelier above you.

12:21.990 --> 12:25.470
Those who have a mark surfacing on the card are challengers.

12:29.710 --> 12:31.040
We'll be back right after this.

12:34.560 --> 12:35.750
Pokémon Quiz!

12:36.110 --> 12:37.060
The answer is...?

12:48.960 --> 12:49.840
A battle, huh?

12:50.150 --> 12:51.160
I prefer this.

12:52.990 --> 12:54.500
This is a good match-up.

12:56.990 --> 12:59.250
Satoshi, Serena, do your best!

13:02.580 --> 13:04.590
I won't lose in a battle either, Serena.

13:05.090 --> 13:05.880
Me neither!

13:06.590 --> 13:08.160
Satoshi, let's do our best.

13:08.160 --> 13:09.470
Yeah, of course.

13:09.940 --> 13:12.750
Oh man, the brats are my opponents?

13:12.750 --> 13:14.150
Don't you even <i>think</i> about losing.

13:16.110 --> 13:17.060
Now then,

13:17.060 --> 13:18.670
start the battle!

13:22.660 --> 13:23.750
Let's go, Eievui!

13:24.910 --> 13:27.370
Pikachu, use Quick Attack on Peroream!

13:32.370 --> 13:33.910
Peroream, Energy Ball!

13:36.110 --> 13:37.410
Eievui, Swift!

13:42.190 --> 13:43.090
Not bad.

13:43.380 --> 13:45.600
Maaiika, use Psybeam on Pikachu!

13:49.330 --> 13:51.390
Pikachu, dodge and use Iron Tail!

13:57.920 --> 13:58.790
Maaiika!

13:59.140 --> 14:00.080
Hat rre you toing?

14:00.590 --> 14:00.900
Sorry...

14:04.270 --> 14:07.950
Good job, Eievui. It seems it is starting to not be bothered by its surroundings any more.

14:07.950 --> 14:08.540
Yeah.

14:08.910 --> 14:10.150
We've only just started!

14:11.570 --> 14:12.950
I expected nothing less from Serena and Satoshi.

14:13.680 --> 14:16.290
I have a plan. Will you work with me?

14:16.660 --> 14:17.540
O-Okay.

14:17.950 --> 14:19.170
First, attack them!

14:19.520 --> 14:20.960
Maaiika, Psybeam!

14:22.160 --> 14:22.720
Dodge!

14:23.870 --> 14:24.800
Cotton Spore!

14:31.120 --> 14:32.430
Once more, please!

14:32.430 --> 14:34.100
Maaiika, Psybeam!

14:39.760 --> 14:40.310
Pikachu!

14:40.640 --> 14:41.250
Eievui!

14:42.820 --> 14:43.910
Now, Tackle!

14:45.250 --> 14:47.050
All right, pummel them!

14:52.100 --> 14:52.610
Pikachu!

14:55.460 --> 14:57.170
Time for the finale!

15:01.360 --> 15:01.910
Eievui...

15:02.390 --> 15:04.570
You're right. Now it's our turn!

15:05.060 --> 15:06.270
Eievui, Swift!

15:08.830 --> 15:09.590
Energy Ball!

15:15.920 --> 15:17.560
Maaiika, Psybeam!

15:22.480 --> 15:23.020
Eievui!

15:23.620 --> 15:25.060
Pikachu, can you continue?

15:28.070 --> 15:28.820
All right!

15:28.820 --> 15:30.690
Pikachu, Electro Ball!

15:33.920 --> 15:35.590
Eievui, are you all right?

15:38.190 --> 15:39.310
Thunderbolt!

15:39.310 --> 15:40.200
Energy Ball!

15:44.770 --> 15:47.880
I'm always powerless in moments like this...

15:48.820 --> 15:53.350
But you know, a certain someone told me that my smile gives others strength.

15:54.450 --> 15:57.850
I don't know how much strength I can give you,

15:58.770 --> 15:59.640
but I <i>want</i> to give you strength.

16:12.710 --> 16:13.460
Could this...

16:13.460 --> 16:14.070
...possibly be...?

16:15.940 --> 16:16.410
It's evolving...?

16:25.990 --> 16:26.910
Nymphia...

16:30.420 --> 16:32.420
Nymphia, the Intertwining Pokémon.

16:32.790 --> 16:37.860
It wraps its ribbonlike feelers around the arm of its beloved Trainer and walks with him or her.

16:39.030 --> 16:39.890
Nymphia...

16:42.270 --> 16:43.520
Nymphia, you're right.

16:43.940 --> 16:45.410
The battle isn't over yet!

16:46.750 --> 16:47.350
Serena.

16:48.100 --> 16:49.650
Satoshi, thanks for the backup!

16:50.370 --> 16:51.140
Pikachu, you too.

16:52.850 --> 16:54.580
We won't lose just because it evolved!

16:54.900 --> 16:56.800
Peroream, Energy Ball!

16:59.540 --> 17:00.010
Dodge!

17:04.210 --> 17:05.460
That is Fairy Wind!

17:05.940 --> 17:06.620
So you've learned that!

17:07.200 --> 17:08.510
That was awesome, Nymphia!

17:10.740 --> 17:12.930
I have a bad feeling about this...

17:13.230 --> 17:14.950
Maaiika, Tackle.

17:23.380 --> 17:25.140
She's right. It <i>is</i> a lovely dance.

17:27.030 --> 17:28.020
Fairy Wind!

17:31.190 --> 17:32.030
Evade it!

17:37.040 --> 17:37.650
Peroream?

17:37.910 --> 17:38.720
Maaiika!

17:39.380 --> 17:41.990
Peroream and Maaiika are unable to battle!

17:42.510 --> 17:45.290
Therefore, the winners are the pair of Satoshi and Serena!

17:46.080 --> 17:51.540
A big applause for the Mesdemoiselles and their partners for showing us a très bien battle!

17:56.420 --> 17:57.920
That was amazing, Serena!

17:58.370 --> 18:00.050
Yeah, thank you!

18:00.350 --> 18:01.710
Congratulations!

18:01.710 --> 18:03.430
A Nymphia, a Nymphia!

18:07.830 --> 18:10.080
To think it actually evolved into a Nymphia...

18:10.430 --> 18:10.750
Huh?

18:11.200 --> 18:17.620
Out of all of Eievui's evolved forms, it needs to be especially attached to its Trainer in order to evolve into a Nymphia.

18:18.030 --> 18:19.030
I had no idea.

18:21.730 --> 18:23.510
Please bear with me, Nymphia.

18:24.190 --> 18:25.760
Geez, what are you doing?

18:25.760 --> 18:26.820
I'm ashamed...

18:29.700 --> 18:30.970
Geez...

18:31.140 --> 18:32.980
Now there's nofing weft but to eat!

18:34.150 --> 18:40.350
Now then, as a special favor to everyone who came today, I will tell you the location of the next Tripokalon.

18:40.650 --> 18:43.470
The next Tripokalon will be in Frey City!

18:44.400 --> 18:44.880
Serena.

18:46.180 --> 18:48.020
Let's compete at the Tripokalon next time.

18:49.890 --> 18:50.230
Yeah.

18:52.800 --> 18:56.710
And see, that girl and her Nymphia were really lovely!

18:57.310 --> 19:00.150
I rarely hear you talking about someone like this.

19:01.950 --> 19:06.510
I'm sure you will think the same when you meet her and her Pokémon, Maestra. They're glittering!

19:06.930 --> 19:08.040
Right, Mafoxy?

19:09.680 --> 19:11.120
I've found someone as well.

19:11.460 --> 19:12.750
You have, Maestra?

19:13.350 --> 19:16.790
It's still touch-and-go with her, but...

19:17.430 --> 19:19.170
...she's a lot like you used to be.

19:19.510 --> 19:21.260
Huh? What do you mean?

19:22.590 --> 19:24.300
It is time for you to leave.

19:25.060 --> 19:25.540
Okay.

19:25.970 --> 19:28.670
Maestra, I'm sorry. I'll call you again.

19:28.950 --> 19:30.560
Sure. Do your best.

19:33.390 --> 19:34.990
We can't fall behind!

19:44.880 --> 19:46.820
Elle-san was lovely, wasn't she?

19:49.140 --> 19:51.200
Nymphia, please bear with me from now on!

19:53.190 --> 19:55.120
Serena, hurry!

19:56.000 --> 19:57.120
Coming!

19:58.960 --> 20:01.470
Unexpected interactions with her rivals...

20:01.920 --> 20:04.500
...and her Eievui's evolution to Nymphia.

20:05.280 --> 20:12.140
Serena and her Pokémon have reached out to each other and made yet another step forward on the stairs towards being a Pokémon Performer.

20:16.100 --> 20:21.060
Sunday January 31st at 8am!

20:16.840 --> 20:18.460
Nicolun and Pokémon Yoga?

20:18.970 --> 20:20.120
On Sunday at 8am!

20:23.290 --> 20:24.970
Performer News!

20:26.590 --> 20:29.610
This show roots for the Pokémon Performers that dream of their future.

20:29.610 --> 20:31.270
It is presented to you by me, Takuro, and...

20:31.270 --> 20:32.370
...me, Yajiko!

20:32.650 --> 20:35.110
Today we'll feature Performers who participated in tournaments!

20:35.110 --> 20:36.150
First is this girl!

20:36.150 --> 20:38.510
Her costume matches the color of Nyaonix-chan's body!

20:38.710 --> 20:39.950
Oh my, so fancy!

20:39.950 --> 20:42.240
This girl wears the same pattern as Rafflesia's flower.

20:42.240 --> 20:43.280
It's elegant and lovely!

20:43.280 --> 20:46.150
Finally, this girl is so fluffy she's a perfect match for Peroppuff!

20:46.150 --> 20:48.090
Oh, so cute! I wanna wear that too!

20:48.090 --> 20:49.720
I'd feel sorry for the outfit if you wore it, Yajiko.

20:49.720 --> 20:52.220
Geez! You deserve a Vital Throw for saying that!

20:52.540 --> 20:54.350
All right, finally, we'll present what we've chosen to be the best clothing match this time!

20:56.030 --> 20:57.880
Today, it's this little Pokémon!

20:58.200 --> 21:01.210
It's Madame Pikachu!

21:09.580 --> 21:11.770
Oh my, it's paralyzing!

21:18.300 --> 21:20.230
All right, everyone! Let's go together!

21:20.430 --> 21:21.510
Towards our next adventure!

21:22.270 --> 21:24.000
After reuniting with Shota we have a battle, but in the middle of it...

21:24.220 --> 21:27.460
Satoshi, that was amazing! Did you just fuse with Gekkouga?!

21:27.460 --> 21:28.570
What? Fuse?

21:28.910 --> 21:30.700
Well, I don't know...

21:30.700 --> 21:32.200
Will you show me again?

21:32.470 --> 21:33.790
Huh? Who are you...?

21:34.090 --> 21:35.420
I'm Alan.

21:36.280 --> 21:38.810
Next time on Pocket Monsters XY&Z:

21:39.160 --> 21:42.280
The Strongest Mega Battle! Gekkouga VS Mega Lizardon!!

21:42.610 --> 21:46.090
Next Time

21:42.610 --> 21:46.090
The Strongest Mega Battle!
Gekkouga VS Mega Lizardon!!

21:43.030 --> 21:44.950
Everyone, get Pokémon!

21:46.120 --> 21:56.120
Next episode:

21:46.120 --> 21:51.080
Satoshi and Alan battle!

21:46.950 --> 21:51.560
Pocket Monsters XY&Z was brought to you by these sponsors.

21:51.150 --> 21:56.120
Something strange happens to Gekkouga again!?
